## New or continuing obligations identified by this audit

The audit does not add a new manuscript primitive beyond the current architecture, but it reinforces the following unresolved implementation tasks:

1. repair the sampled institutional fixed-point operator;
2. establish canonical kernel hierarchy and common comparison spaces;
3. select canonical theorem sources and mark duplicate drafts superseded-but-preserved;
4. integrate the expanded failure taxonomy;
5. preserve attainment/closure caveats in value-of-information claims;
6. retain pathwise rather than pointwise chance-safety semantics;
7. merge nonlinear-transition conjectures;
8. preserve discrepancy-coverage requirements.

## Publication conclusion

The audit's original two-paper recommendation is not adopted as a current instruction. Its valid conceptual and mathematical points are assigned to the master architecture and source-level theorem registry. No legitimate content is discarded.
